From 7e423428fb8442d09e5c5c51f68d0ba02225b862 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 05:26:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Support No Disc with a closed tray

With no image mounted, libretro always reported an open tray and
rejected every out-of-range image index. Frontends could not leave an
empty drive closed, and list edits could turn No Disc into a real slot.

Track the tray separately and normalize out-of-range selections to the
image count. Preserve that selection when entries are added or removed,
and reset disc control state before loading another game. Keep the
physical shell state separate from the latched Getstat status so the
existing disc-swap delay still works. Synchronize the tray with restored
media after loading an existing state.

Tested single-CHD and two-disc Metal Gear Solid loads, empty-drive
transitions, removal, refill and game reload. Direct CD-ROM checks cover
reset, Getstat during a subimage swap, and loading old open/closed tray
states. The patch builds and passes these checks on the upstream base
without the other fixes.
